              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 7.7(b): Land breeze"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.598,
            0.084,
            0.884,
            0.269
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "At night, the process reverses. In the absence of sunlight, land cools down faster than the water in the sea. As a result, the air above the sea is warmer and rises up. Cooler air from the land then moves towards the sea, creating a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "land breeze",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (Fig. 7.7b)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.597,
            0.27,
            0.883,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, people living near the seashore experience that the direction of the wind reverses in the day and night."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.363,
            0.472,
            0.388
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.3 Radiation"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.403,
            0.244,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.107,
                0.403,
                0.244,
                0.565
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.408,
            0.882,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you remember when Pema and Palden were sitting around the fireplace? They felt warm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.279,
            0.465,
            0.437,
            0.518
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "I wonder how heat from the fire reaches us?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.451,
            0.447,
            0.883,
            0.54
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Their grandfather tells them that the heat transfer, in this case, takes place directly from the fire (hot object) to us by a process known as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "radiation",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". The heat of the Sun reaches us through this process. Heat"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.539,
            0.762,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "transfer by radiation does not require any medium."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.56,
            0.883,
            0.636
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "All objects radiate heat. You must have observed that a hot utensil kept away from the flame cools down after some time. What is the reason for it? The hot utensil cools down by radiating heat to its surroundings."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.68,
            0.277,
            0.713
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "D IVE EEPER"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.07,
            0.657,
            0.301,
            0.855
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
